WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.282
This static pivot creates three diagnosis columns.

00:00:03.282 --> 00:00:07.762
It works well when those categories are intentionally selected and stable.

00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:10.357
The advantage is a predictable schema.

00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:16.172
The limitation is that any new diagnosis category will not automatically appear as a new column.

00:00:16.172 --> 00:00:23.207
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:23.207 --> 00:00:26.582
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:32.292
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:32.292 --> 00:00:33.075
combination.
